Download jenkins and nginx
	>> jenkins --> used to create ci cd pipelines 
	>> nginx --> one of the web Server

>> sudo docker pull jenkins
>> sudo docker pull nginx

>> sudo docker run -d nginx  // d --> detached mode, will not stop the current command prompt. [this containers runs background

>> sudo docker ps ---> can check if the container is running or not
>> sudo docker container inspect 9d // to go inside the container [9d is the 2 character of container id] display all details about the container

>> curl http://172.12.0.2:80 --> IP address and port --> this is actually a website

To execute the outside in the browser, we have to use port binding
	>> sudo docker run -d -p 3600:80 --name subha-nginx nginx
		3600 --> port you want to listen to
		:80 ---> is the port where the application is running 
		subha-nginx --> name that it should run
		nginx is the actual image name
	>> get the IP address, from details in the lap.. access column except  port, give port as 3600

